{"parentUuid":"7f09dd1d-40a4-45c3-9f6d-c9555256fbf8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"adfaf6893cfeed936","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018X9yidyss2VzWd8tcC2R65","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936\nf860ff3 codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\nbd7e1e2 rules: a recording outranks a doc; partial support is supported with deviations; unsupported may be shown by runs (#90)\ncfd2711 rules: judge per unit (subjects), module.yaml is the agent's, module-distinct (#89)\nstatement: >-\n  The session can be compacted on request; hooks fire before and after the\n  compaction, and the hook before it can stop it.\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#precompact\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#postcompact\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact-nohooks\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          /compact is a slash command, and no mock parses one: a scenario's compact\n          control record requests the compaction, so PreCompact's custom_instructions\n          is always null and the text a user passes after /compact is not modeled.\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no API and no context window, so it never compacts by\n          itself and never meets a context-limit error: an automatic compaction is\n          requested by a scenario, and the variant where blocking an automatic\n          compaction that was triggered to recover from a context-limit error\n          surfaces that error is not modeled. A blocked automatic compaction is\n          skipped and the conversation continues uncompacted.\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go      | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n codex-mock/internal/events/stream.go               |  7 ++-\n .../snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/run.yaml      |  2 +\n .../shell-exit-status/samples/20261003-142833/SEAL |  6 ++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/events.jsonl           | 22 +++++++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/exit.txt               |  1 +\n .../samples/20261003-142833/payloads.jsonl         |  6 ++\n .../samples/20261003-142833/stderr.txt             |  1 +\n .../samples/20261003-142833/stream.jsonl           | 16 +++++\n ...8-34-01a1022a-acf2-7e12-9814-d1750d3ff095.jsonl | 28 +++++++++\n .../snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh |  5 ++\n .../runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json        | 24 ++++++++\n .../runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt        |  1 +\n spec/capabilities/bash-tool-result.yaml            | 16 ++++-\n 14 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\nCLA.md\nCONTRIBUTING.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\nadr\nclaude-mock\ncodex-mock\ncursor-mock\ngo.mod\ngo.sum\ninternal\nproposals\nspec\ntools","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2a6b1cf7-bab8-476b-9120-60eb903fd27c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:45:55.691Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f09dd1d-40a4-45c3-9f6d-c9555256fbf8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitB