{"parentUuid":"296094af-2eda-451e-ad7b-acf460738599","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"adfaf6893cfeed936","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QiWdpMmjWmGbzWdiRH3pWV","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# The ONLY writer of codex-mock/snapshots/ (the snapshots-read-only gate\n# refuses every other write). Everything it writes is sealed; snapshots-current\n# refuses a snapshot whose seal does not match, so a hand edit is caught at the\n# commit even if it slipped past the gate.\n#\n#   capture.sh run <name>    run the scenario in runs/<name>/setup/ against the\n#                            real `codex exec`, and add a sample\n#   capture.sh doc <url>     freeze a doc page (e.g. https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks):\n#                            its sha256 goes in the MANIFEST; its text only into a cache\n#                            under the git dir, never into the repo\n#   capture.sh drop <run> <ts>  remove one sample (a bad or non-hermetic capture)\n#   capture.sh all           re-capture every run and doc at the installed\n#                            codex's version, and set MANIFEST.version to it\n#\n# A scenario is hand-authored, and only its setup/ is:\n#   runs/<name>/setup/prompt.txt       the prompt\n#   runs/<name>/setup/hooks.json       the user layer's $CODEX_HOME/hooks.json\n#   runs/<name>/setup/hook.sh          optional: the hook every event runs;\n#                                      it appends its stdin to $HOOK_LOG\n#   runs/<name>/setup/args             optional: extra codex exec flags, one per line\n#   runs/<name>/setup/env              optional: KEY=VALUE lines codex inherits on\n#                                      top of the hermetic env (e.g. an outer session's)\n#\n# Authentication: codex has no headless login but the user's. The run's fake\n# CODEX_HOME holds ONLY a symlink to the logged-in auth.json (the same trick as\n# claude-mock's Keychains link): nothing is copied, and a token codex refreshes\n# during the run is moved back over the original, so the login stays valid.\n# The link is gone with the fake home, and a capture is refused if any token\n# value reached the sample.\nset -euo pipefail\nhere=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nmanifest=\"$here/MANIFEST.yaml\"\ndie() { echo \"capture.sh: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nversion() { yq -r '.version' \"$manifest\"; }\ninstalled() { codex --version | awk '{print $2}'; }\nauth_src=\"${CODEX_AUTH_JSON:-$HOME/.codex/auth.json}\"\n# The first capture creates the MANIFEST, frozen at the installed version: it is\n# a snapshot file too, so nothing else may write it.\n[ -f \"$manifest\" ] || printf 'version: \"%s\"\\n' \"$(installed)\" >\"$manifest\"\n\n# One capture at a time: they are real model calls on one account.\nlock=/tmp/capture-codex.lock.d\nacquire() { local i=0; until mkdir \"$lock\" 2>/dev/null; do i=$((i + 1)); [ \"$i\" -le 600 ] || die \"another capture holds $lock\"; sleep 1; done; }\n\n# seal DIR — SEAL lists the sha256 of every other file under DIR.\n# Written to SEAL.tmp and renamed only on success, so a SEAL always means a\n# complete sample (the cleanup trap relies on it).\nseal() { (cd \"$1\" && find . -type f ! -name 'SEAL*' | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs shasum -a 256 >SEAL.tmp && mv SEAL.tmp SEAL); }\n\n# normalize — hook payloads and event-stream frames into events.jsonl: what a\n# scenario did, without what differs between two captures of the same\n# behaviour (ids, paths, timings, the model's own wording).\n# The run's own session (thread) id is kept as <SESSION_ID> wherever it appears\n# (a payload's session_id, a child's env, a command's output): that they match\n# is recorded, the value itself is not.\nnormalize() {\n  local cap=\"$1\" sid\n  sid=\"$(jq -r 'select(.session_id) | .session_id' \"$cap/payloads.jsonl\" 2>/dev/null | head -n1 || true)\"\n  jq -c --arg sid \"${sid:-<none>}\" 'walk(if type == \"object\" then del(.transcript_path, .cwd, .turn_id, .tool_use_id, .uuid,\ncodex-mock/snapshots/runs:\nhook-exit-codes\nhook-exit-json\nhook-matchers\nhook-timeout\nhook-unstartable\nnested-session-env\nposttool-block\npretool-decisions\nprompt-blocked\nsession-end\nshell-exit-status\nstops\nsubprocess-session-env\n\ncursor-mock/snapshots/runs:\nadditional-context\nfile-tools\nhook-exit-codes\nhook-fail-closed\nhook-json-nonzero\nhook-matchers\nhook-timeout\nhooks-together\nnested-session-env\npretool-refusal\nsession-start-block\nshell-exit-status\nsubprocess-session-env\nsymlinked-cwd\ntool-failure\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh\nnew file mode 100755\nindex 0000000..89d1231\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hook.sh\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+#!/bin/sh\n+# Every event logs its payload.\n+IN=$(cat)\n+printf '%s\\n' \"$IN\" >>\"$HOOK_LOG\"\n+exit 0\ndiff --git a/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7c54628\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/hooks.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+{\n+  \"hooks\": {\n+    \"PostToolUse\": [\n+      {\n+        \"hooks\": [\n+          {\n+            \"type\": \"command\",\n+            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n+          }\n+        ]\n+      }\n+    ],\n+    \"Stop\": [\n+      {\n+        \"hooks\": [\n+          {\n+            \"type\": \"command\",\n+            \"command\": \"\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\"/hook.sh\"\n+          }\n+        ]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\ndiff --git a/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f0d3b37\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status/setup/prompt.txt\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+Make every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another command or put in a script. Run these shell commands one at a time, in order, whatever happens: 1) grep zzz /dev/null 2) sh -c 'echo SOME-OUTPUT; exit 1' 3) sh -c 'echo MORE-OUTPUT; echo ERR-OUTPUT >&2; exit 2' 4) sh -c 'exit 3' 5) echo FINE. Then reply only DONE.\ndiff --git a/spec/capabilities/bash-tool-result.yaml b/spec/capabilities/bash-tool-result.yaml\nindex 0093ac4..c94ef36 100644\n--- a/spec/capabilities/bash-tool-result.yaml\n+++ b/spec/capabilities/bash-tool-result.yaml\n@@ -13,7 +13,21 @@ providers:\n     runs:\n       - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bashfail\n       - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n-  codex: pending\n+  codex:\n+    docs:\n+      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse\n+    runs:\n+      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/shell-exit-status\n+    deviations:\n+      - adr: capability-grounding\n+        statement: >-\n+          Codex does not make a failed command an error result for the agent:\n+          what it is told is the command's output alone, the same text a\n+          success would have, with no exit code stated and none marked as an\n+          error (recorded: runs/shell-exit-status). The failure is shown only\n+          in the event stream's command_execution item, whose status is\n+          \"failed\" and whose exit_code and aggregated_output carry the exit\n+          status and what the command printed, and the mock does the same.\n   cursor:\n     docs:\n       - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#aftershellexecution\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8d336ae5-78bf-4fc8-83e8-e0e500d199fb","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:46:05.741Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"296094af-2eda-451e-ad7b-acf460738599","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"claude/capabilities-matrix-impl-2a0cfd"}
