R that fits (e.g. capability-grounding) or drop the modeled-surface citation. (file-guard \"adr-conformance\")\n  - The docs (hooks#sessionstart) say a SessionStart hook with source \"compact\" returns additionalContext that is delivered to the continuation after compaction, and the mock models SessionStart:compact, but no test under hook-additional-context/codex (TestHookAddedContextIsKept) checks that context from a compact-source SessionStart is added; the PostToolUse context test also never covers a failed (non-zero exit) Bash call, and the multi-hook 'all kept' check covers only UserPromptSubmit with a loose Contains.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/stderr.txt (and 42 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestT017_07_Compaction (sr:proves manual-compaction/claude) pins the /compact local-command-caveat record to \"Caveat: The messages below were generated by the user while running local commands. DO NOT respond...\", but the recorded transcript in runs/compact (2.1.285) holds \"<local-command-caveat>The command below was run directly in Claude Code, not sent to you as a request, and its output goes straight to the user. It's recorded here as context for later messages.</local-command-caveat>\"; also no test asserts the hook_started/hook_response frames the compact run streams around a compaction when hooks are configured. The codex subjects were not evaluated.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/stderr.txt (and 42 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd only checks that the reasons appear somewhere in the rollout file, that there are 3 Stop events and that there is 1 turn.completed. It never asserts the doc claim that the reason becomes a new user prompt the agent receives (the recorded runs show further agent_message items after each block). It does not check that the exit-2 stderr reason is delivered separately from the JSON reason, or that the Stop that blocks leaves the turn running. It also does not exercise the doc line that continue:false overrides a block.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/stderr.txt (and 42 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The codex docs (hooks#stop, lines 1071-1075) list `turn_id` (active Codex turn id) as a Stop payload field, and TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing never asserts it. Its `last_assistant_message` check is also not backed by the recording, because the runs/stops Stop payloads contain only `stop_hook_active`. The null case of `last_assistant_message` (documented as `string | null`) is not tested either.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/stderr.txt (and 42 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - The single test, TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses, leaves documented variants and recorded outcomes unchecked. (1) The docs JSON forms are not tested: hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext for adding context and {decision:block, reason} for refusing; only plain-text stdout and exit 2 are exercised. (2) The refusal check in prompt-blocked is too loose: it asserts only the stream shape thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed, and does not assert that the echo SHOULDNOTRUN tool never ran, that no agent message was produced, or that the UserPromptSubmit payload had the prompt, hook_event_name and permission_mode fields. (3) The statement clause about firing for a background-task notification has no test. (4) The cannot-rewrite claim is covered only indirectly by the prompt=[the prompt] line.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/stderr.txt (and 42 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go (`if tu.Name == compactTool { h.compact(ctx, tu.Input); return }`) with control_compact.go (`const compactTool = \"Compact\"`) silently decides how a scenario script asks a mock for a harness-level action (here, a compaction): it reserves a pseudo tool_use name that is intercepted outside the scenario module. claude-mock already makes the same choice differently, with a `{\"type\":\"compact\"}` control record routed by the scenario module (claude-mock/internal/runner/record.go, stream_scan.go), and cursor-mock will face it next. The question is: how does a scenario script trigger mock-level control actions (a control record, or a reserved tool name)? Checklist of the other choices: ResumeLast in internal/compaction/run.go is local and falls under module internal/compaction; hooks.Stops and the PreCompact/PostCompact events and payload are covered by module internal/hooks; session.Compacted is a local rollout record grounded in a recording (adr/capability-grounding); the e2e and unit tests are local. No ADR decides this. Ask the user to decide it (a new ADR), or which existing ADR it falls under. (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\n  - Home glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go is too wide: control.go (handleControlRecord dispatching worktree_create/worktree_remove/subagent_start control records) belongs to the subagents/hooks concern, and control_fork.go (claudeForkSchema, forkSegment) belongs to the session concern (forking a session), not to the compaction sequence; narrow the glob to control_compact.go, control_boundary.go, control_frames.go and control_summary.go, or move those two files to their owning modules.\nThe files this refusal is about: internal/compaction/module.yaml (file-guard \"module-distinct\")\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"11667599-5582-4b6e-af4e-080858db6f05","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:24:19.688Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"044f1a10-6182-4c20-865e-d2681281c8fd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aa43418fbebf671c6"}
