{"parentUuid":"ddf26068-d558-4309-aff2-8ccd7d27baf7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"adfaf6893cfeed936","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0134nVJ9E4AD4XTztxRc3PK4","type":"tool_result","content":"Could not apply 8bdf79c... codex: a scenario asks for a compaction with a compact control record; a stopped one aborts the turn\nthe following rules refused this work:\n  - The docs (hooks#sessionstart) say a SessionStart hook with source \"compact\" returns additionalContext that is delivered to the continuation after compaction, and the mock models SessionStart:compact, but no test under hook-additional-context/codex (TestHookAddedContextIsKept) checks that context from a compact-source SessionStart is added; the PostToolUse context test also never covers a failed (non-zero exit) Bash call, and the multi-hook 'all kept' check covers only UserPromptSubmit with a loose Contains.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestT017_07_Compaction (sr:proves manual-compaction/claude) pins the /compact local-command-caveat record to \"Caveat: The messages below were generated by the user while running local commands. DO NOT respond...\", but the recorded transcript in runs/compact (2.1.285) holds \"<local-command-caveat>The command below was run directly in Claude Code, not sent to you as a request, and its output goes straight to the user. It's recorded here as context for later messages.</local-command-caveat>\"; also no test asserts the hook_started/hook_response frames the compact run streams around a compaction when hooks are configured. The codex subjects were not evaluated.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopBlockContinuesTheTurnWithOneEnd (capabilities_test.go:250) only checks that BLOCK-JSON-REASON and BLOCK-EXIT2-REASON appear as substrings anywhere in the rollout; it never asserts the reason is handed to the agent as a new user-role continuation prompt, or that the agent ran again after each block (the stops sample shows agent_message items after the blocks before the single turn.completed), so it would still pass if the mock logged the reasons without feeding them back.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestStopPayloadCarriesLastMessageAndContinuing never checks the Stop payload's doc-listed turn_id (Active Codex turn id; nothing in the stop tests asserts it on Stop), never checks the third recorded Stop (stop_hook_active true after a second consecutive block, only 2 Stops are driven), and never covers last_assistant_message being null when unavailable.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - TestUserPromptSubmitAddsContextOrRefuses never tests the documented JSON forms of the hook (hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext adds developer context; {\"decision\":\"block\",\"reason\":...} refuses the prompt), and it does not test the background-task-notification case the statement names. Its refusal check (replay of prompt-blocked) asserts only the stream shape [thread.started, turn.started, turn.completed]. It does not assert that the scenario's tool command (echo SHOULDNOTRUN) never ran, that the agent never received the prompt, or that the exit-2 stderr reason (PROMPT-BLOCK-MSG) is handled as the reason, so a mock that ran the agent but streamed no events would also pass.\nThe files this refusal is about: codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/compaction_test.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/config.go, codex-mock/internal/hooks/payload.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/control_compact.go, codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/run.yaml, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/SEAL, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/events.jsonl, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/exit.txt, codex-mock/snapshots/runs/manual-compaction-auto-blocked/samples/20261003-145328/payloads.jsonl (and 43 more) (file-guard \"capability-rigor\")\n  - codex-mock/internal/runner/turn_host.go (`if tu.Name == compactTool { h.compact(ctx, tu.Input); return }`, with `const compactTool = \"Compact\"` in control_compact.go) makes an undecided choice about the scenario wire format: how does a scenario script ask a mock for a harness action that is not an agent tool call? Here a reserved tool_use name is intercepted before the tool path. claude-mock does the same thing with a `{\"type\":\"compact\"}` control record (claude-mock/internal/runner/record.go, stream_scan.go). So the mocks now disagree, and the next control (cursor compaction, worktree or subagent controls in codex) will copy one of the two. Neither the internal/scenario module nor any ADR decides this. Ask the user to decide it (a new ADR), or which existing ADR it falls under. Every other choice is local or covered: Stops/payload tweaks (module internal/hooks), Steps.ResumeLast (module internal/compaction), File.Compacted (module internal/session), and the tests (local). (file-guard \"concern-undeclared\")\n  - The glob claude-mock/internal/runner/control*.go is too wide: control.go handles worktree_create/worktree_remove/subagent_start control records (subagents concern), and control_fork.go (forkSegment/claudeForkSchema, used by session_fork.go) implements session forking (session concern); narrow the glob to the compaction files (control_compact.go, control_boundary.go, control_frames.go, control_summary.go) or move those two files to the subagents and session modules.\nThe files this refusal is about: internal/compaction/module.yaml (file-guard \"module-distinct\")\nEND\n\n[exited with code 0]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"93ddc1fa-daef-4ccb-ac67-5da699d4ab1a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:39:13.406Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ddf26068-d558-4309-aff2-8ccd7d27baf7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
