{"parentUuid":"3db5c043-9825-45bd-a0be-0c8ef0447892","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"adfaf6893cfeed936","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UCaa5SYk5UGEiJrXd4rdHb","type":"tool_result","content":"Check every file-guard over merge-base(--base, --head)..--head, deterministically.\n\nOnly reads: it never executes a script, a judge or a requirement and never writes. It computes each\nsubject's key (running the rule's subjects script, without a session) and reads the stored verdict, so the\nsame repository state and the same stored results read the same anywhere. A key with no stored verdict is\nred (\"not judged yet\", run sr-checks run); a stored fail shows its reasons. A citation requirement counts a\nSloprail-Cites-* trailer on the commit that last really changed the file, which is checkable from the repository\nalone.\n\nPrints each subject's latest result, then each refusal. Exits 0 when everything passes, 1 when\nanything fails or has no result.\n\nUsage:\n  sr-checks verify --base <rev> --head <rev> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --base string   The base revision: a branch, tag or sha (required)\n      --head string   The head revision: a branch, tag or sha (required)\n  -h, --help          help for verify\n      --json          Print the per-subject results as JSON\nname: sloprail\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\njobs:\n  sloprail-verify:\n    name: sloprail verify\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha || github.sha }}\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@v5\n        with:\n          go-version: '1.25'\n      - run: GOBIN=\"$HOME/.local/bin\" go install github.com/sloprail/sloprail/services/sr-checks@2ce91382fdedf42c010056b7807ccc5f15e89948\n      # sr-mark: ci-verify\n      - env:\n          EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n          BASE_REF: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.ref }}\n          PR_HEAD: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\n          BEFORE: ${{ github.event.before }}\n        run: |\n          if [ \"$EVENT\" = pull_request ]; then\n            ~/.local/bin/sr-checks verify --base \"origin/$BASE_REF\" --head \"$PR_HEAD\"\n          else\n            # new branch / force push: before is all zeros or a missing object -> merge-base with the default branch, else the root commit\n            if [ -z \"${BEFORE//0/}\" ] || ! git cat-file -e \"$BEFORE^{commit}\" 2>/dev/null; then\n              BEFORE=$(git merge-base origin/main \"$GITHUB_SHA\" 2>/dev/null || git rev-list --max-parents=0 \"$GITHUB_SHA\" | tail -1)\n            fi\n            ~/.local/bin/sr-checks verify --base \"$BEFORE\" --head \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n          fi","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"beccdcf6-992e-4f2a-8198-2c75a7fefb02","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:04:00.957Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3db5c043-9825-45bd-a0be-0c8ef0447892","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-adfaf6893cfeed936","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a11c0a040e3cf682b"}
